===Etymology===
{{dercat|en|gmw-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|Wales}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Wealas|Wēalas}}, plural of {{m|ang|wealh||Celt, Welsh person}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*walhaz||Celt, Roman}}. Compare the second element in {{l|en|Cornwall}}, and also {{l|en|Gaul}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|wālz|a=UK,US}}, {{IPA|en|/weɪlz/|[weɪɫz]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Wales.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪlz|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|whales|wails}} (''whales'' in accents with wine-whine merger)

